# Site theme

All visual work on this site must follow the theme in `@src/theme.css`. That file is the source of truth for color, type, space, shape, motion, and reusable classes.

Do this before adding or restyling any page, section, or component:

1. Read `@src/theme.css`.
2. Reuse existing tokens and primitives.
3. Only then write page-specific layout CSS.

## Stack and style approach

- Plain global CSS plus CSS custom properties. Do not add Tailwind, CSS-in-JS, or a UI library.
- Page layout stays in files like `@src/App.css`. Tokens and shared classes stay in `@src/theme.css`.
- Fonts (Fraunces + Outfit) are loaded in `@index.html`. Do not swap families.
- Compose classes in markup the way `@src/App.tsx` already does (`section prose`, `hero__cta btn`, `display rise-in`).

## Use these primitives

| Class | Use for |
| --- | --- |
| `.section` | Centered content block |
| `.prose` | Body copy |
| `.display` | Fraunces brand heading |
| `.headline` | Outfit medium subhead |
| `.lede` | Supporting text |
| `.btn` | Primary CTA |
| `.rise-in` | Enter animation; stagger with `--delay` |

Example for a new section:

```html
<section class="section prose">
  <h2 class="headline">Title</h2>
  <p class="lede">Supporting line.</p>
  <p>Body copy.</p>
  <a class="btn" href="#next">Continue</a>
</section>
```

## Tokens, not one-off values

- Use CSS variables from `:root` in `@src/theme.css` (`--paper`, `--ink`, `--accent`, `--foam`, `--display`, `--sans`, `--space-*`, `--radius`, and the rest).
- Do not introduce new hex, rgb, font-size, or spacing values when a token already exists.
- If a new value is truly needed, add a named token to `@src/theme.css` first, then use the variable.
- Keep the look: paper/ink surfaces, teal accent, foam text on hero, square corners (`--radius: 0`), no drop shadows, 720px layout breakpoint.

## Do not

- Invent a parallel palette, type scale, or button style.
- Round corners, add shadows, or restyle `.btn` unless the request is explicitly to change the theme.
- Copy Vite/React scaffold colors (purple/cyan) into the UI.
